---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact TRACED | Corrections and Source Questions"
  description="Contact TRACED for breach archive corrections, source questions, privacy questions, or responsible notes about public breach data."
>
  <Nav currentPath="/contact/" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="contact-page">
    <section class="contact-panel reveal">
      <span class="contact-kicker">TRACED CONTACT</span>
      <h1>Corrections, source questions, and privacy notes</h1>
      <p>
        Jonathan R. Reed runs TRACED: a public breach archive with a password exposure checker attached. If a case file
        needs a correction, a source needs clarifying, or you have a privacy concern, send the note through his main
        site.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-actions">
        <a href="https://jonathanrreed.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JonathanRReed.com</a>
        <a href="https://helloworldfirm.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hello World Coding</a>
      </div>
      <p class="contact-note">
        Do not send passwords, private keys, personal documents, or breach samples through a contact form. TRACED does not
        need sensitive material to answer archive corrections or source questions.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-details">
        <p>
          Useful correction notes include the case name, the public source that should be checked, and a short description of
          what looks inaccurate. For privacy questions, include only the minimum context needed to understand the concern.
        </p>
        <p>
          TRACED does not investigate private account ownership, remove records from Have I Been Pwned, or accept raw breached
          data. All it does is put the public record somewhere readable and point you toward better credential habits.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a source link changes, include the original case URL, the replacement public reference, and the reason the
          archive should be updated. If the issue is about a password check, describe the browser behavior without sending
          the password, hash, or any private account identifier.
        </p>
        <p>
          It helps to keep source corrections separate from personal support requests. A case title, date, data-class label,
          source reference, or explanatory note can all be fixed when the public record backs the change. What can&apos;t happen
          is confirming whether a specific person was in a breach, or removing anything from the original HIBP dataset.
        </p>
        <p>
          For bug reports, include the page URL, your browser, your device, and exactly what you saw happen. Broken navigation,
          controls you can&apos;t reach, wrong schema, missing context, dead external links: all of that is worth sending, and
          none of it requires anything sensitive.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .contact-page {
    min-height: 72vh;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    padding: 7rem 2rem 5rem;
  }

  .contact-panel {
    max-width: 720px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .contact-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .contact-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .contact-actions a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .contact-actions a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .contact-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .contact-details {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .contact-page { padding: 6rem 1rem 4rem; }
    .contact-panel { padding: 1.25rem; }
  }
</style>
